{
  "$schema": "./schema/scoring.schema.json",
  "design_notes": [
    "Team Sync meter of design section 11.2, score formula of 11.3 and grades of 11.4. All numbers are game values (section 19: \"Score weights & grades\").",
    "Team Sync: the design lists gains for Gold, Silver, Bronze and a Good Call, none for Platinum; Platinum is a Gold with every player perfect, so it is read as the Gold gain. The design does not say whether the meter resets after a Mission Control Moment.",
    "Formula: Mission Score = (sum of the components) × difficulty multiplier × score boosts. \"Remaining budget % × 1,000\" and \"schedule margin % × 500\" are read as the fraction (0 to 1) times the points, so 30% of the budget left gives 300 points; the grade thresholds only make sense with that reading. Kind per_fraction.",
    "\"Secondary up to 1,500\" and \"Science / Data (contract-specific, up to 1,500)\" are upper limits (kind up_to); the design does not say how the points divide over two or three secondary objectives or how each contract earns science points.",
    "Teamwork pays per minigame by tier and 20 points per Good Call. Knowledge pays 50 per correct prediction and 30 per trivia tiebreak; Appendix A shows a correct Predict answer as \"+50 KP\".",
    "The difficulty multiplier is not repeated here: it is score_multiplier of the assist level flown (data/assist_levels.json: Cadet 0.8, Engineer 1.0, Flight Director 1.25). The score-boost multiplier is the Score Multiplier boost of data/boosts.json, which applies per segment and is capped at ×1.5.",
    "Grades: D is \"< 4,000 or crew lost\", so it has no min_score and crew_lost_grade is D (5.2: the grade is capped at D if the crew is lost)."
  ],
